      "answer": "Celiac disease damages the small intestine and interferes with the absorption of nutrients from food [1]. This damage and malabsorption create wide-ranging problems in many systems of the body [2]. The inflammation and malabsorption occur in the digestive system, specifically in the small intestine [1, 2, 3].",
